From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 20:08:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 015/260] [ae-patch] Use Tabler icons for project icons instead
 of emojis

The project icon picker (New project, the rename dialog, the new-chat
landing header) now offers the Tabler outline set (tabler.io/icons, npm
@tabler/icons 3.46.0) in place of emoji-mart: a search box over names,
categories and tags, an 8-column grid, arrow keys, Enter and Space, and
Up from the top row back to the search box. It fills the height the
callers' popovers already publish in --emoji-picker-height, so it fits a
390px phone and scrolls inside.

A Tabler pick is stored as tabler:<name> in the project's config.icon,
which the server keeps as a free string. Emoji values saved before keep
rendering as text; no icon is still the folder; a name the set does not
know falls back to the folder.

Lazy, not curated: the outline shapes (1.2 MB, 231 KB gzipped) load as
one chunk the first time a tabler: icon renders, and the search tags
(1.1 MB, 183 KB gzipped) load only when the picker opens. The main entry
grows by 6.6 KB (2.2 KB gzipped); emoji-mart's two lazy chunks (506 KB,
110 KB gzipped) are no longer emitted. Rows draw a same-size empty box
until the shapes arrive. The data comes from @tabler/icons rather than
@tabler/icons-react because the React package ships one module per icon
(its dynamic-imports map points at .ts files missing from dist in
3.46.0) and carries no tags; both files sit outside the package's
exports map, so they are reached with import.meta.glob on the installed
path, which also keeps tsc from typing 2 MB of JSON.

Logic lives in new files: web/src/lib/aeTablerIconData.ts (the two lazy
loaders), web/src/lib/aeTablerIcon.tsx (the value format and the
renderers) and web/src/components/AeTablerIconPicker.tsx (the picker),
each with a vitest suite. Upstream files change by a few lines each:
ProjectIconPicker.tsx (EmojiPicker renders the Tabler picker; the
landing tile draws the glyph; its popover gets the default card chrome),
ProjectPicker.tsx (one branch in ProjectRowIcon), NewProjectButton.tsx
and Sidebar.tsx (the glyph in the icon tiles and the project folder
header), ProjectIconPicker.test.tsx (the stubbed picker), package.json
and pnpm-lock.yaml (@tabler/icons). The emoji-mart dependencies stay:
@lobehub/fluent-emoji still depends on them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
